<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's Foxtel plans to hike pay TV fee by A$3.</title>
<headline>Australia's Foxtel plans to hike pay TV fee by A$3.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian pay television operator Foxtel said on Monday that it will increase the cost of its basic package by A$3 to A$42.95 per month from August 29, increasing the number of channels it offers at the same time.</p>
<p>Foxtel, which is owned by News Corp Ltd and the Australian government's Telstra Corp, has about 200,000 subscribers and is one of the two largest pay TV operators alongside Optus Vision.</p>
<p>Foxtel said this is the first increase since it started business nearly two years ago.</p>
<p>The number of Foxtel channels will be raised to 28 from 26.  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
